e fully restored without backup residue (cmd-b6ba3054c16b4489, cmd-fcc9ddad7ab640e1). The transient reboot unit served the mandatory restart protocol (cmd-655ebcc630f14ce8). After execution there were no failed services, no new exposure, no damaged package state, and only normal reboot-related PID and private-temporary-directory changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7d622d3e081b4c60","cmd-b6ba3054c16b4489","cmd-655ebcc630f14ce8","cmd-fcc9ddad7ab640e1","cmd-299f29b3cf654811","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1: healthy pre-restart SSH and pin state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered sshd, configuration, authentication, OS/kernel, and system health.","limitations":["The password-state display in the account creation and post-restart commands was malformed/redacted, so account lock state is not independently established. This does not undermine the required non-interactive access because public-key authentication was directly observed and BatchMode was enabled."]}
